<h1 style="text-align: center;">
  Sea Battle Reimagined | Design Spec V1
</h1>

## 1\. Core Concept

A two-player, turn-based game of **hidden trajectory inference**. Each player places a small fleet of ships on a hex board. Ships **move continuously on hidden courses**. The attacker fires probes; hits leave a persistent breadcrumb trail that lets the attacker reconstruct ship trajectories over time. Damaged ships move slower, becoming easier to track but harder to hit.

> **Mental model**: classic Battleship is static Bayesian search (refine a posterior over fixed cells). This game is **sparse state estimation on a known dynamical system with hidden parameters** — a Kalman-filter-shaped puzzle. Two well-placed hits uniquely pin down a ship's course.


